## How to apply

1. Look up the real UID on device (see section above if present).
2. Edit the `currentUid` field in:
   - `profile.kernelsu.json`
   - `profile.ksu-next.json`
   - `profile.sukisu-ultra.json`
   (All three are byte-identical apart from the `target_fork` field — pick whichever fork you're running.)
3. Push the matching JSON to your device:
   ```sh
   adb push profile.<your_fork>.json /data/local/tmp/profile.json
   ```
4. Apply via the matching apply script (audit-only — read it first):
   ```sh
   bash apply.<your_fork>.sh
   ```
5. Verify:
   ```sh
   adb shell su -c 'id -Z'    # Should show u:r:ksu:s0 (or your custom domain)
   adb shell su -c 'capsh --print'    # Should show the capabilities you granted
   ```

